<article> <header class="hero"> <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"> <a href="/">Home</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <a href="/glossary">Glossary</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <span>TwnNm and Ctry</span> </nav> <div class="hero-badge"><span class="pulse-dot"></span><span style="position:relative;z-index:1">Glossary · Elements</span></div> <h1><span class="accent">TwnNm and Ctry</span></h1> <p class="page-meta">Glossary entry · Last reviewed 26 July 2026</p> <!-- ANSWER BLOCK — picked up by speakable schema --> <p class="answer-block"><strong><code>&lt;TwnNm&gt;</code> (Town Name, max 35 characters)</strong> and <strong><code>&lt;Ctry&gt;</code> (Country, an ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 code)</strong> are the two mandatory structured elements of every compliant ISO 20022 postal address from 15 November 2026. They are classified <strong>R — Required</strong> in the CPMI harmonised data model and together constitute the minimum-viable postal address.</p> </header> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">In Practice</div> <h2 class="section-title">How TwnNm and Ctry works in practice</h2> <div class="content-block"><p>The rationale is regulatory screening: the EPC notes that only the structured Town and Country fields are needed for it, and FATF Recommendation 16 sets name plus Town Name and Country as the beneficiary minimum. <code>&lt;TwnNm&gt;</code> must carry a non-placeholder value; <code>&lt;Ctry&gt;</code> must match <code>[A-Z]&#123;2&#125;</code>.</p></div> <p class="src">Source: CPMI harmonisation requirements — technical annex §0.26 / §0.30 / p5; EPC 153-22 v2.1; the ioNova Postal Address Specification v2.0 Appendix I Q1; Table 22 (§10.2.1).</p> <div class="content-block"><p>The minimum-viable postal address:</p></div>
<div class="code-block"><pre><span class="cmt">&lt;!-- Minimum-viable postal address --&gt;</span>
<span class="tag">&lt;PstlAdr&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;TwnNm&gt;</span>WELLINGTON<span class="tag">&lt;/TwnNm&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;Ctry&gt;</span>NZ<span class="tag">&lt;/Ctry&gt;</span>
<span class="tag">&lt;/PstlAdr&gt;</span></pre></div> <div class="content-block"><p>Parent reference: <a href="/address-intelligence/structured-address-mandate">ISO 20022 structured address mandate</a>.</p></div> </section> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">Citations</div> <h2 class="section-title">Sources</h2> <div class="sources-list"> <h3 class="sources-subhead">Standards &amp; regulatory sources</h3>
